Abstract Abstract A family of disjoint pairs of finite sets \mathcal{P}=\{(A_{i},B_{i})\mid i\in[m]\} is called a Bollobás system if A_{i}\cap B_{j}
eq\emptyset for every i
eq j , and a skew Bollobás system if A_{i}\cap B_{j}
eq\emptyset for every i<j . Bollobás proved that for a Bollobás system, the inequality \sum_{i=1}^{m} inom{|A_{i}|+|B_{i}|}{|A_{i}|}^{-1}\leqslant 1 holds.
